I opened the session in `.claude/worktrees/people-cleanup` (branch `session/people-cleanup`). Two sub-agents are running:

- **Matcher fix:** a participant with a date of birth will be looked up by last name and date of birth instead of by email. That stops a child registered by a different parent from getting a second person row.
- **Design doc** (`.claude/plans/people-cleanup.md`) for #133 and #137. It covers:
  - the cleanup surface: a Directus extension, or a `duplicate_person` audit finding with a merge action;
  - a merge that handles every link that points at a person;
  - whether the ~200 existing duplicates can be merged in bulk;
  - how Clubspot updates and staff corrections live together on the same fields.

I'll review the fix and read the design before bringing either back to you.

